        <Options>
            <Main applyHouseholdOperatingConditions="false" applyReducedOperatingConditions="false" atypicalElectricalLoads="false" waterConservation="false" referenceHouse="false">
                <Vermiculite code="1">
                    <English>Unknown</English>
                    <French>Inconnu</French>
                </Vermiculite>
            </Main>
            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>Air Leakage Locations:



Back Bedroom window and around window frame.



Kitchen window



Bathroom Fan has excessive air leakage when not in operation. Damper may have failed or did not ever have one installed. Also around the fan itself is not sealed well. Unit should be replaced and properly installed and sealed.



Utilidor is very leaky and not sealed well.



Back door needs new weather stripping.



Electrical Panel is not sealed properly.



Electrical receptacles on exterior walls are not sealed well



</airSeal>
                <ceilings>Add minimum of R-25 to the exisitng ceiling insulation. There are lots of ceiling leaks so would recommend a layer of spray foam along bottom of attic to help with air leakage. Replace Bathroom fan before doing this.



Please refer to Artic Energy Alliance for rebates on insulation upgrades and the criteria for these products.</ceilings>
                <foundation>Add R-12 Batt on top of the R-20 batt in he crawlspace floor. Would also recommend adding R-15 EPS to the bottom side of the house as well.



Please refer to Artic Energy Alliance for rebates on insulation upgrades and the criteria for these products.</foundation>
                <windows>Upgrade windows to ENERGY STAR® Zone 3 rated.



Make the back bedroom and kitchen windows a priority.



Please refer to Artic Energy Alliance for rebates on windows/doors and the criteria for these products.

</windows>
            </RURComments>
        </Options>
